BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Morehead Planetarium & Science Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261006T190000
DTSTAMP:20261003T010330
CREATED:20260904T151803Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T152044Z
UID:40228-1791309600-1791313200@moreheadplanetarium.org
SUMMARY:Carolina Science Cafe: Who’s a Journalist in the Age of AI?
DESCRIPTION:Who’s a Journalist in the Age of AI? \n\n\n\nTheorizing Distributed Journalistic Authority Amid Newsfluencers\, Algorithms\, and Generative Systems \n\n\n\nWho’s a Journalist in the Age of AI? addresses a critical development in the news media. In this talk\, UNC-Chapel Hill’s Hussman School of Journalism and Media faculty member\, Deb Aikat\, PhD\, will discuss how generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) reconfigures the epistemic boundaries of journalistic authority\, credibility\, and public verification in democratic discourse.  \n\n\n\nDr. Aikat will discuss how AI is reshaping press freedom at a time when public trust in media has sunk to 28%\, according to Gallup’s 2025 survey. He studies the shifting information landscape in the U.S. and India — the world’s oldest and largest democracies — tracing how digital platforms empower people to publish\, protest\, and participate in civic life beyond traditional newsrooms. \n\n\n\n\n\nDesigned for adults\, Carolina Science Cafe is a free program that explores science topics making national and international headlines\, offering the chance to meet the experts behind the work. This special program is hosted at Haw River Tap & Table in Carrboro on the first Tuesday of every month. Light appetizers are available for all attendees. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout the Speaker\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDr. Deb Aikat is a professor in the UNC Hussman School of Journalism and Media. \n\n\n\nA former journalist\, Deb Aikat (pronounced EYE-cut)\, is a tenured full professor in the UNC-Chapel Hill Hussman School of Journalism and Media who is reimagining the future of a free press in the age of AI. \n\n\n\nAikat theorizes how artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming the free press as a democratic institution. When Deb arrived at UNC-Chapel Hill in 1995\, the internet was still new terrain. He launched the journalism school’s first online course and helped build what would become the university’s online master’s program in digital communication. Three decades later\, he’s studying one of the biggest transformations to ever face the news industry: generative AI.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\nMore about Dr. Aikat\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCarolina Science Cafe is produced by Morehead Planetarium and Science Center and sponsored by the UNC Chapter of Sigma Xi.
URL:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/calendar/carolina-science-cafe-whos-a-journalist-in-the-age-of-ai/
LOCATION:Haw River Tap & Table\, 300 E Main St C\, Carrboro\, NC\, 27510\, United States
CATEGORIES:Teen And Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://moreheadplanetarium.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Carolina-Science-Cafe-1920x842-1.jpeg
END:VEVENT
